"""English report for the completed eight-query hybrid-pool experiment."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];HERE=ROOT/'round2';OUT=HERE/'hybrid-pool-8-v1'
def main():
 e=json.loads((OUT/'evaluation.json').read_text());p=json.loads((HERE/'hybrid-pool-plan.json').read_text());m=e['metrics']
 lines=['# BM25 + vector candidates -> hosted Jev: equal-budget result','','**The tested hybrid pool performed worse than either single retriever followed by Jev on this eight-query panel.** At the same20-candidate budget, hybrid -> Jev reached Recall@5 **0.541667**, versus **0.645833** for BM25 -> Jev and **0.666667** for vector -> Jev. The hybrid lost a relevant vector candidate before reranking. This is a negative finding for this fixed round-robin construction, not proof that all hybrid retrieval is worse.','',
 '## Matched comparison','','| Candidate construction | Unreranked R@5 | Unreranked R@10 | Jev R@5 | Jev R@10 | Jev NDCG@10 | Pool recall@20 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm in ['bm25','vector','hybrid']:
  a=m[arm+'_control']['aggregate'];b=m[arm+'_jev']['aggregate'];lines.append('| '+arm+' | '+' | '.join(f'{v:.6f}' for v in [a['Recall@5'],a['Recall@10'],b['Recall@5'],b['Recall@10'],b['NDCG@10'],a['Recall@20']])+' |')
 lines+=['','| Candidate construction | Unreranked NDCG@10 | Oracle R@5 | Oracle R@10 | Oracle NDCG@10 |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm in ['bm25','vector','hybrid']:
  a=m[arm+'_oracle']['aggregate'];lines.append('| '+arm+' | '+' | '.join(f'{v:.6f}' for v in [m[arm+'_control']['aggregate']['NDCG@10'],a['Recall@5'],a['Recall@10'],a['NDCG@10']])+' |')
 lines+=['','True recall counts retrieved positive qrels divided by **all positive qrels for each query**, then macro-averages over the same eight queries. Completeness is separately available in the evaluation JSON. Oracle values use labels only after predictions and describe pool ceilings, not deployable predictions. All24calls succeeded; no failures were removed. The fixed evaluation also retains invalid/unattempted queries with empty rankings and zero scores rather than substituting retrieval fallback.','',
 '## What was frozen before labels and calls','','Eight queries were selected by a fixed salted SHA256 order, excluding the128-query scorer cohort, prior selective/fusion/clause panels and the untouched six-query prompt-confirmation panel. The public benchmark has nevertheless been historically exposed; this is not a genuine blind final test. The IDs, exact requests, source ranking hashes, corpus hash, pools and scoring rule are preserved in `hybrid-pool-plan.json` and `prepared-hybrid-pool.json`.','',
 '- **BM25:** cached top20.','- **Vector:** cached SkillRet-Embedding0.6B top20.','- **Hybrid:** alternate BM25 then vector items from their cached top100 lists; deduplicate by skill ID; stop at exactly20. The same interleaved order is the unreranked hybrid control.','',
 'Every arm uses20unique candidates, complete public name/description evidence, the same original four-level Score rubric, pinned hosted model `jev-1.13.0`, descending returned score and original candidate-order tie breaks. Call order rotates across queries to reduce fixed temporal bias. **Candidates are combined before Jev. No post-Jev rank fusion is applied.** This is distinct from earlier vector+Jev RRF experiments.','',
 'There were no identical historical request hashes to reuse. The runner also supports reuse of exact successful requests within the run and refuses uncertain identical requests rather than blindly retrying. Actual execution used24newcalls x20questions =480typed questions. No prompt/pool tuning or second batch followed the results.','',
 '## Per-query gains and losses','','| Hybrid versus | Metric | Mean delta | Wins / ties / losses |','|---|---|---:|---|']
 for comparison,metrics in e['comparisons'].items():
  for metric,v in metrics.items():lines.append('| '+comparison.replace('hybrid_vs_','')+' | '+metric+' | '+f"{v['mean_delta']:+.6f}"+' | '+' / '.join(map(str,v['wins_ties_losses']))+' |')
 lines+=['','The major loss versus vector is **q-02374**: the relevant skill `cf819299-bcd3-4f41-8bbc-c5b7615783b8` was vector rank12 and BM25 rank25. It survived vector top20 but was excluded from the20-slot interleaved hybrid pool. Recall@5 and Recall@10 each dropped from1to0 for this query. The other seven queries tied vector on recall; hybrid slightly improved NDCG on q-04449.','',
 'Versus BM25 -> Jev, hybrid lost Recall@5 on q-02485 (-0.5) and q-00970 (-1/3), with six ties and no wins. At Recall@10 it lost only q-00970. Thus losses involve both retrieval coverage and placement within the first five; pool construction and reranking are not interchangeable explanations. Full per-query controls, pool hits, oracle ceilings and outcomes are in `hybrid-pool-8-v1/per-query.csv` and `evaluation.json`.','',
 'A larger union would change the candidate budget, so it was not substituted after seeing the loss. Other hybrid constructions or cohort sizes remain untested. No general superiority claim or statistical certainty is warranted from eight cases.','',
 '## Latency, cost and safeguards','','| Arm | Calls | Input tokens | Metered USD | Median batch seconds |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
 for arm,t in e['timings'].items():lines.append(f"| {arm} | {t['new_calls']} | {t['input_tokens']:,} | {t['metered_usd']} | {t['median_api_seconds']:.3f} |")
 resource=e['resources']
 lines+=['',f"Total: **24/24successful calls, {e['known_input_tokens']:,}input tokens, USD{e['known_usage_usd']} metered usage** at the pinned USD0.042/million input rate. The full USD0.10reservation remains committed; total commitments are **USD1.97 / USD4**. Cumulative known usage is USD{e['cumulative_known_usage_usd']}, excluding the earlier uncertain OpenRouter call. Cash billing was not verified; the user-reported signup credits were not queried. No top-up.", '',
 'Timings measure same-size20-question API batches and include client/network time; differing description lengths cause token differences. Retrieval used cached rankings, so these are not end-to-end retrieval latencies. No new embeddings, model downloads or GPU inference occurred.', '',
 f"Resource guard exited normally: host minimum {resource['host_min_available_gib']:.3f}GiB available, guest {resource['guest_min_available_gib']:.3f}GiB, GPU minimum free {resource['gpu_min_free_mib']}MiB, maximum GPU temperature {resource['gpu_max_temp_c']}C, no active swap. The monitor is stopped. WSL responsiveness settings were unchanged.", '',
 '70offline tests pass, including hybrid deduplication, balanced disjoint pools, overlap and shortfall handling. The result audit checks request hashes, candidate IDs, score ordering, token totals and per-query full-denominator recall. All raw predictions are retained. Other paid work remains paused; there is no automatic follow-up.','',
 '## Reproducibility and handoff','','From `/home/user/code/mia5150-local`: `.venv/bin/python round2/score_hybrid_pool.py` and `.venv/bin/python round2/report_hybrid_pool.py` regenerate the analysis without network calls. `.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s round2 -p "test_*.py"` runs offline tests. Do not rerun the one-shot paid worker.','',
 f"Protocol SHA256: `{e['protocol_sha256']}`.",f"Raw results SHA256: `{e['results_sha256']}`.",'',
 'This English report is ready for the existing MIA5150 Notion page. No upload, external publication or Git push was performed by this task. The current result supersedes no previous cohort: earlier six-query rubric results, two-query local model diagnostics and vector/Jev fusion results remain separate evidence.']
 (HERE/'HYBRID_POOL_RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
 print(json.dumps({'report':str(HERE/'HYBRID_POOL_RESULTS.md'),'status':'completed_negative_hybrid_result','calls':e['calls'],'cost_usd':e['known_usage_usd'],'shared_commitments_usd':'1.97'}))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
